      short: 'Blocking V2 lowers the cAMP that drives cyst growth: cysts grow more slowly.',
      def: 'Tolvaptan in autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease with rapid progression (Mayo 1C–1E).',
      mech: 'ADH, through V2 and cAMP, stimulates cyst proliferation and secretion. V2 blockade slows kidney growth and GFR loss.',
      dx: 'Aquaresis (polyuria, nocturia, thirst), hepatotoxicity (monthly transaminases for the first 18 months), dehydration if the patient does not drink.',
